    "description": "Pattern (both instances today on epam/dmtools-dart: #424 ~16:37Z, #419 ~17:2xZ): a rework leg no-ops correctly (fix already pushed by operator, GraphQL thread census = 0 unresolved), but the gh-957 no-op loop guard still fires rework-loop-escalated after 2 zero-commit/zero-thread legs. The escalated label then wedges the SM's validate-armed pointer: every PR behind it logs '⏳ FIFO-queued (awaiting validate-armed turn)' and the merge slot never arms — queue-wide stall until a human clears the label.\n\nSuggested guard refinement: do NOT escalate when (a) the GraphQL unresolved-thread census is 0 AND (b) the PR head carries no red validation (no validation_failed / failing head checks) — in that state the correct move is to re-dispatch VALIDATION, not park the PR. Also consider excluding escalated PRs from blocking the armed pointer (skip-and-continue instead of head-of-line block)."
  }
